<section class="utility-head"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">FAQs</div><h1 class="h1">Clear Answers, Without the Ceremony</h1><p class="lead">The FAQ should solve problems quickly. It does not need to audition for a wedding magazine cover.</p><div class="search-box"><input placeholder="Search FAQs"><a class="btn secondary" data-action="Prototype search only.">Search</a></div></div></section><section class="section tight"><div class="container"><div class="utility-panel"><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q"><span>How does eJuno help couples today?</span><span>+</span></div><div class="faq-a">eJuno brings together venue discovery, wedding services, planning tools, inspiration and support across its current public experience.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q"><span>Can I book or enquire through eJuno?</span><span>+</span></div><div class="faq-a">Where the current eJuno journey supports enquiry or booking, the redesigned interface continues into that existing flow.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q"><span>Does this redesign add new product functionality?</span><span>+</span></div><div class="faq-a">No. V4 changes the experience layer and visual organisation. Backend-dependent actions remain current functionality or are clearly simulated in the prototype.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q"><span>Is the design locked to Italy forever?</span><span>+</span></div><div class="faq-a">No. The current content can remain Italy-led while the visual system and information architecture are scalable to additional markets later.</div></div><div style="margin-top:24px"><a class="btn primary" href="/pages/contact">Contact eJuno</a></div></div></div></section>

